Looks like the enemy is defensive
Let's go 5 cycle their flag

>(>++[...-].[+++++------])*21

Current losses/problematic enemies:
3pass: misdetection that can't be corrected without losing to other programs
defend13/14: misdetection on one polarity
double_tripwire_avoider: designed to counter this program among others
elliott's stupidly long name: loses on one polarity due to misdetection
lead_acetate_philip: correctly detected by opponent
sexyghoul/spookygoth: insufficiently predictable
speedy2/3: has no counterstrategy
superfast_jellyfish: has no counterstrategy
wiggle3: misdetection; but it wins anyway on one polarity due to backup lock


